diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..b61627c 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,20 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+A session can supply a default timeout for all its requests::
+
+    with requests.Session(timeout=(3.05, 27)) as session:
+        r = session.get('https://github.com')
+        r = session.get('https://github.com', timeout=5)
+        r = session.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
+        session.timeout = 10
+
+Omitting ``timeout`` uses the current value of ``session.timeout``, which
+defaults to ``None``. An explicit timeout overrides that default for one
+request, and an explicit ``None`` disables it. This also applies when sending
+a prepared request with ``Session.send``. Redirects retain the timeout selected
+for the initial request, even if the session default changes during the chain.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
